    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Give the Israelites the following laws: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LEV.25.39+LEV.25.40+LEV.25.41+LEV.25.42+LEV.25.43+LEV.25.44+LEV.25.45+LEV.25.46"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lev 25.39–46",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If you buy a Hebrew slave, he shall serve you for six years. In the seventh year he is to be set free without having to pay anything. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If he was unmarried when he became your slave, he is not to take a wife with him when he leaves; but if he was married when he became your slave, he may take his wife with him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If his master gave him a wife and she bore him sons or daughters, the woman and her children belong to the master, and the man shall leave by himself. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if the slave declares that he loves his master, his wife, and his children and does not want to be set free, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "then his master shall take him to the place of worship. There he is to make him stand against the door or the doorpost and pierce his ear. Then he will be his slave for life.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If a man sells his daughter as a slave, she is not to be set free, as male slaves are. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If she is sold to someone who intends to make her his wife, but he doesn't like her, then she is to be sold back to her father; her master cannot sell her to foreigners, because he has treated her unfairly. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If a man buys a female slave to give to his son, he is to treat her like a daughter. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If a man takes a second wife, he must continue to give his first wife the same amount of food and clothing and the same rights that she had before. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If he does not fulfil these duties to her, he must set her free and not receive any payment.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
