            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If some men are fighting and hurt a pregnant woman so that she loses her child, but she is not injured in any other way, the one who hurt her is to be fined whatever amount the woman's husband demands, subject to the approval of the judges. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if the woman herself is injured, the punishment shall be life for life, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LEV.24.19+LEV.24.20"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lev 24.19–20",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "DEU.19.21"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Deut 19.21",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "MAT.5.38"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Mt 5.38",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "burn for burn, wound for wound, bruise for bruise.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.25"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If someone hits his male or female slave in the eye and puts it out, he is to free the slave as payment for the eye. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If he knocks out a tooth, he is to free the slave as payment for the tooth.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If a bull gores someone to death, it is to be stoned, and its flesh shall not be eaten; but its owner is not to be punished. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if the bull had been in the habit of attacking people and its owner had been warned, but did not keep it penned up — then if it gores someone to death, it is to be stoned, and its owner is to be put to death also. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "However, if the owner is allowed to pay a fine to save his life, he must pay the full amount required. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If the bull kills a boy or a girl, the same rule applies. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If the bull kills a male or female slave, its owner shall pay the owner of the slave thirty pieces of silver, and the bull shall be stoned to death.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.32"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If someone takes the cover off a pit or if he digs one and does not cover it, and a bull or a donkey falls into it, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "he must pay for the animal. He is to pay the money to the owner and may keep the dead animal. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If someone's bull kills someone else's bull, the two of them shall sell the live bull and divide the money; they shall also divide up the meat from the dead animal. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 21:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if it was known that the bull had been in the habit of attacking and its owner did not keep it penned up, he must make good the loss by giving the other man a live bull, but he may keep the dead animal.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.21.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.21.36"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
